error[E0409]: `.0` cannot be applied to `(int, int) ! {none}`
 --> mem:///main.lu:7:13
  |
7 |     let a = t.0
  |             ^ this is `(int, int) ! {none}`
  |
  = note: a `!T` is two values, never one, and no operator reads it ([type.row.operand]): a member
    read and a method call read their base as an operator reads its operand, and `?`, `else`
    and `match` are the whole of how a row is handled. Handle it first — `t?.0`, `(t else
    …).0` — and read what it yields.
